  "question": {
    "text": "If the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math> touch the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> at the points where the curve intersects&nbsp;the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math> is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, points are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
